WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.540
There's a lot going on in Rick and Morty,
with its dimension-spanning adventures involving

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:07.890
Szechuan sauce and catchphrases like "wubba
lubba dub dub.”

00:00:07.890 --> 00:00:11.139
It's a complicated show to jump on board with
from the get-go.

00:00:11.139 --> 00:00:15.009
So to help newcomers and those who need a
refresher, let's explain the otherworldly

00:00:15.009 --> 00:00:16.870
story of Rick and Morty.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:20.230
To be clear: We're going to spoil everything
that's happened on the show so far.

00:00:20.230 --> 00:00:21.390
So there's your warning.

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.390
"Uh-oh!

00:00:22.390 --> 00:00:23.390
Spoilers!"

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:24.390
Meet Rick and Morty

00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:27.039
Let's start with Rick Sanchez, the smartest
man in the universe.

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:30.830
Rick only recently reunited with his adult
daughter, Beth Smith.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.680
Because she's desperate for her dad's approval
and traumatized by him leaving in the first

00:00:34.680 --> 00:00:38.550
place, Beth welcomes his dysfunction into
the home she shares with her husband, Jerry,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.380
a perpetually down-on-his-luck loser who Rick
hates.

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:43.539
Beth and Jerry have two kids.

00:00:43.539 --> 00:00:47.400
Their daughter, Summer, is in many ways the
average American teenage girl.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:51.530
She's worried about fashion, her friends,
and the various boys she likes at her school.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.469
What sets her apart from the rest of her peers
is how utterly unfazed she seems to be by

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:59.370
her parents failing marriage and her grandpa's
high-risk space adventures.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:04.699
Then there's Morty, the youngest in the family
and Rick's closest ally in his maddening adventures.

00:01:04.699 --> 00:01:09.500
Prior to Rick's arrival, Morty was a troubled
kid charting well below average at his school.

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:14.100
A big reason why could have to do with his
crippling crush on a girl named Jessica.

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:19.010
After Rick shows up, well, none of that really
changes, but Morty's life becomes very different.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.520
"It's just Rick and Morty!

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.630
Rick and Morty and their adventures, Morty!

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:26.259
Rick and Morty forever and for 100 years,
Rick and Morty's things!

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:28.370
Me, and Rick and Morty, runnin' around!"

00:01:28.370 --> 00:01:29.370
Thinking with portals

00:01:29.370 --> 00:01:32.950
The first episode of the series opens with
Morty falling asleep at the breakfast table

00:01:32.950 --> 00:01:37.790
after a drunk Rick kept him up the night before
with threats to restart humanity with a neutrino

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:38.790
bomb.

00:01:38.790 --> 00:01:40.970
Yes, that's the first thing that happens.

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:44.750
Morty's parents worry that Rick's hijinx with
their son are having unhealthy affects on

00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:49.320
him, particularly at school, where they acknowledge
he may be developing slower than his peers.

00:01:49.320 --> 00:01:54.009
But Rick nonetheless takes Morty out of school
for an adventure using his famous portal gun:

00:01:54.009 --> 00:01:57.200
a handheld device that allows him to travel
anywhere in space.

00:01:57.200 --> 00:02:00.070
It can also travel between infinite alternate
dimensions.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:04.940
So, while Rick can't travel in time, he can
travel in different timelines.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:08.600
The show doesn't shy away from the impact
that traveling multiple universes can have

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:11.000
on even a super-genius' mind.

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:15.360
It's revealed in episode one that it's hard
for Rick to relate to other people, even his

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:19.320
family, because he knows that the best and
worst versions of himself exist in infinite

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:20.470
realities.

00:02:20.470 --> 00:02:24.640
The adventure goes horribly, and it's pretty
traumatic for Morty, who breaks his legs and

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:27.300
is forced to kill some alien officers.

00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.750
When it's over, Rick explains to Beth and
Jerry that traveling with him is the only

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:33.370
way a mind like Morty is going to catch up
in school.

00:02:33.370 --> 00:02:35.200
Of course, that's not really true.

00:02:35.200 --> 00:02:36.230
"Holy cow, Rick!

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:40.010
I didn't know hangin' out with you was makin'
me smarter!"

00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:41.410
"Full disclosure, Morty: It's not."

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:42.520
The Cronenberg incident

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:46.090
Things go terribly awry when Morty's crush
on Jessica becomes overwhelming.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:50.480
He asks his grandpa Rick if there's anything
he can create to make her like him.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:54.480
Although Rick thinks his grandson is being
creepy, he relents and gives Morty a love

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:55.510
potion of sorts.

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:58.250
But there's a drawback: it's contagious.

00:02:58.250 --> 00:03:02.250
Morty uses it on Jessica at the annual Flu
Season Dance, and it causes her to spread

00:03:02.250 --> 00:03:06.720
an uncontrollable virus that makes people
aggressively in love with Morty, regardless

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:08.760
of gender, age, or status.

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:13.540
So Rick makes two attempts to produce an airborne
cure that not only makes it spread globally,

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:18.810
but it mutates everyone into hideous monsters
that Rick offhandedly labels "Cronenbergs."

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:23.230
To escape the escalating problem, Rick transports
Morty and himself to a nearly identical version

00:03:23.230 --> 00:03:27.440
of that timeline where a parallel Rick and
Morty both die in a freak accident after that

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:30.500
universe's Rick successfully solves the Cronenberg
problem.

00:03:30.500 --> 00:03:35.070
Together, our "heroes" bury their alternates'
corpses and rejoin this alternate version

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.970
of Earth as if nothing ever happened.

00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:38.790
"The answer is don't think about it.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:40.650
It's not like we can do this every week, anyways.

00:03:40.650 --> 00:03:42.820
We get three or four more of these, tops."

00:03:42.820 --> 00:03:43.820
Dysfunctional dimension

00:03:43.820 --> 00:03:47.760
The Smith family has a lot of problems, with
deep-seated resentments in Beth and Jerry's

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:48.810
marriage.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:52.630
Everything gets thrust out into the open in
episode eight after Rick gets frustrated at

00:03:52.630 --> 00:03:57.510
The Bachelor and upgrades the family cable
box with wacky channels from every possible

00:03:57.510 --> 00:03:58.510
dimension.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:04:00.840
While that leads to some very funny alternate-universe
ads...

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.750
"It's two brothers...and they're gonna...it's
called Two Brothers.

00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:05.750
Two Brothers.

00:04:05.750 --> 00:04:08.480
It's just called Two Brothers!"

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:13.200
...it also gives them a glimpse into a world
in which Jerry is as famous as Tom Hanks.

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:18.190
So while Rick and Morty sit on the couch and
watch trashy TV, the rest of the family decides

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:22.200
to watch what alternate, seemingly happier
versions of themselves are doing.

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:25.410
Jerry and Beth discover they could have lived
their personal dreams in a world where they

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:26.930
never had Summer.

00:04:26.930 --> 00:04:30.820
While her parents wonder if their continued
marriage is a good thing for anyone involved,

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:35.030
Summer prepares to run away from home, having
seen what her existence does to them.

00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:39.320
However, Morty stops her by sharing the fact
that he's her brother from a different reality.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:44.100
Her existence, like everything else, is neither
a burden nor an asset, it all means nothing.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:48.160
Meanwhile, Beth and Jerry see themselves get
back together in their otherwise happy alternate

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:49.960
timeline and agree to stay married.

00:04:49.960 --> 00:04:51.151
Every Rick needs a Morty

00:04:51.151 --> 00:04:54.840
A group of Ricks from various universes and
their Mortys has gotten together to form a

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:57.220
society on a floating space citadel.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:02.680
Our Rick, from universe C-137, isn't too much
of a joiner, and he has rebuffed their invitation.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:07.880
But the Council of Ricks comes calling when
a Rick from another dimension frames C-137

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:11.080
Rick for the death of 27 alternate dimension
Ricks.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:15.630
C-137 is arrested by the Council for the crimes
and subsequently escapes.

00:05:15.630 --> 00:05:19.550
That's when Morty learns that Rick's genius
gives off a very distinct brainwave pattern

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:23.160
that makes it easy for his various enemies
to track him.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:25.510
Traveling with Morty is a selfish necessity
for Rick:

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:29.200
"Ricks have a very distinctive and traceable
brainwave due to our genius.

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:32.480
The best way to hide from an enemy's radar
is to stand near someone with complementary

00:05:32.480 --> 00:05:34.300
brain waves that make ours invisible."

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:39.590
While C-137 Morty stages a Morty rebellion
in light of that revelation, our Rick learns

00:05:39.590 --> 00:05:42.120
about the frame-up and Evil Rick is killed.

00:05:42.120 --> 00:05:46.500
The Council then learns that Evil Rick's Morty
was controlling the situation the whole time.

00:05:46.500 --> 00:05:51.080
C-137 Rick and Morty aren't privy to that
information, and Evil Morty vanishes into

00:05:51.080 --> 00:05:52.500
the crowd at the Citadel.

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:53.500
Rick's greatest enemy

00:05:53.500 --> 00:05:58.400
The Galactic Federation, comprised of more
than 6,000 Earth-like planets, is run predominantly

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:01.810
by a bug-like alien race known as the Gromflomites.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:06.360
The Federation is a beacon of order, civilization,
and stability within the universe.

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.650
Obviously, these principles are grating to
the rebellious Rick, along with his friends,

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:12.310
Birdperson and Squanchy.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:15.690
Birdperson invites the Smiths to his wedding
to Summer's friend, Tammy.

00:06:15.690 --> 00:06:19.560
There, he reveals that he and Rick fought
many battles against the Federation and committed

00:06:19.560 --> 00:06:21.840
many atrocities for which they're wanted.

00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.950
"The galactic government considers us terrorists.

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:29.370
It's unwise of me to share these details,
but I've become inebriated."'

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.360
And that's when the Federation launches an
attack orchestrated by Tammy, a deep cover

00:06:33.360 --> 00:06:35.840
Federation operative who kills Birdperson.

00:06:35.840 --> 00:06:37.710
Earth is no longer safe.

00:06:37.710 --> 00:06:41.889
The Smiths go into hiding, and Rick learns
just how much of a burden he's been to his

00:06:41.889 --> 00:06:42.889
relatives.

00:06:42.889 --> 00:06:46.250
Under the guise of going out for ice cream,
Rick reveals his location to the Federation

00:06:46.250 --> 00:06:49.350
on the condition that his family will be allowed
to go free.

00:06:49.350 --> 00:06:52.970
The Smiths are picked up from their hiding
place and return to Earth, which is thriving

00:06:52.970 --> 00:06:54.400
under Federation rule.

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.820
Meanwhile, Rick is seen being locked away
in the bowels of the Gromflomites' most secure

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:02.340
prison, with nothing but time working against
him as they try to unlock his secrets.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:03.530
Fall of the Federation

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:07.580
Rick finds himself inside a Gromflomite simulation
generator as they attempt to trick him into

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:10.350
giving up the secret to interdimensional travel.

00:07:10.350 --> 00:07:14.410
The machine uses Rick's memories against him
and allows the Gromflomites to trigger thoughts

00:07:14.410 --> 00:07:16.550
about how he invented his portal gun.

00:07:16.550 --> 00:07:20.740
Instead of falling for their trick, Rick flexes
his genius and fabricates an origin story

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:24.870
in place of an actual memory, thus hacking
the machine and allowing him to switch bodies

00:07:24.870 --> 00:07:26.220
with his interrogator.

00:07:26.220 --> 00:07:30.180
Meanwhile, Morty and Summer are finding a
Rick-less, Federation-controlled Earth too

00:07:30.180 --> 00:07:31.460
much to bear.

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:35.880
Summer digs up the dead Rick from the Cronenberg
debacle and uses his portal gun, which the

00:07:35.880 --> 00:07:37.780
Council of Ricks flags.

00:07:37.780 --> 00:07:41.610
When Morty and Summer explain that their Rick
had been arrested by the Federation, the Council

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:46.110
dispatches soldiers to assassinate Rick C-137
once and for all.

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:50.080
Rick switches bodies again with one of the
assassin Ricks and uses him to infiltrate

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:51.080
the Citadel.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:55.430
He teleports the citadel into the same space
as the Federation prison, launching a massive

00:07:55.430 --> 00:07:57.360
battle between his two greatest enemies.

00:07:57.360 --> 00:08:02.110
He then reunites with Morty and Summer before
executing the final part of a plan that began

00:08:02.110 --> 00:08:04.460
when he turned himself in after the wedding.

00:08:04.460 --> 00:08:09.040
Rick hacks into the Federation mainframe and
reduces the value of its currency to zero.

00:08:09.040 --> 00:08:12.130
Chaos ensues, and the Federation falls within
minutes.

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:15.300
Defeated, they leave Earth, and Rick returns
home safely.

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.300
Family fractured

00:08:16.300 --> 00:08:20.730
Rick toppling the Federation has an extremely
negative impact on Jerry, who was thriving

00:08:20.730 --> 00:08:22.930
under a government that valued thoughtlessness.

00:08:22.930 --> 00:08:27.060
He realizes that things have gotten much worse
for him now that Rick has replaced him as

00:08:27.060 --> 00:08:30.430
the family patriarch and makes a "him or me"
ultimatum.

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:31.740
It doesn't work.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:37.039
"Jerry's going to spend some time...divorced."

00:08:37.039 --> 00:08:41.050
Having just defeated the Gromflomites and
the Council, an arrogant Rick confesses to

00:08:41.050 --> 00:08:43.990
Morty that this was his grand plan all along.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:47.920
Jerry and the Federation wanted him gone,
so he made them both go away.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.130
Jerry tries his best to not let his depression
get the better of him, including a messy rebound

00:08:52.130 --> 00:08:55.960
with an alien huntress that he meets on an
interdimensional dating app.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:59.640
Beth, meanwhile, can't seem to find her place
in her now fully broken family.

00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:00.790
Evil Morty returns

00:09:00.790 --> 00:09:05.320
The Citadel is not some perfect utopia: it
has a sizable class and wealth divide among

00:09:05.320 --> 00:09:07.850
the various Ricks and Mortys that live there.

00:09:07.850 --> 00:09:11.901
Some versions of Rick wind up doing menial
tasks to keep the Citadel running, and some

00:09:11.901 --> 00:09:16.270
Mortys take a dark turn toward crime while
others thrive without Ricks.

00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:20.140
Evil Morty has been consolidating his power
during the rebuilding of the Citadel following

00:09:20.140 --> 00:09:24.250
the battle with the Federation, adopting a
working-class hero persona that's made him

00:09:24.250 --> 00:09:26.690
popular enough to run for president.

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:30.980
Although his candidacy is first considered
a joke due to the fact that he's a Morty,

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:34.720
Evil Morty gives an impassioned speech about
the class divide in the Citadel.

00:09:34.720 --> 00:09:39.420
"The division I see is between the Ricks and
Mortys that like the Citadel divided, and

00:09:39.420 --> 00:09:40.820
the rest of us."

00:09:40.820 --> 00:09:44.780
With that speech, he becomes the first democratically
elected Morty president.

00:09:44.780 --> 00:09:48.750
However, when it's revealed that a shadow
government exists within the Council, Evil

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:52.490
Morty promptly dispatches all of the Ricks
that threaten his power.

00:09:52.490 --> 00:09:55.190
Evil Morty morphs the Council of Ricks into
a dictatorship.

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.320
Rick's power struggle

00:09:56.320 --> 00:10:01.620
C-137 Rick's propensity to see past traditional
labels and power dynamics puts him directly

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.750
in the crosshairs of the president of the
United States.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:08.680
Always one for an adventure, Rick routinely
takes calls from the "most powerful" man in

00:10:08.680 --> 00:10:13.010
the world because he feels like Morty is enamored
with the idea of helping his country.

00:10:13.010 --> 00:10:17.560
However, when even Morty realizes that they've
basically become the president's intergalactic

00:10:17.560 --> 00:10:21.350
exterminators, they bail on a mission from
the commander-in-chief in favor of playing

00:10:21.350 --> 00:10:22.350
Minecraft.

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.350
"Notify the president."

00:10:23.350 --> 00:10:24.520
"What do I tell him?"

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:25.940
"Tell him the truth.

00:10:25.940 --> 00:10:29.589
Tell him Rick and Morty just blew off America."

00:10:29.589 --> 00:10:33.230
The president is desperate to prove that he
doesn't need Rick and Morty, but he keeps

00:10:33.230 --> 00:10:37.960
coming up short and becomes increasingly erratic
as he constantly loses to Rick.

00:10:37.960 --> 00:10:42.070
Things devolve into a literal fist fight with
the president that ends in a draw when Rick

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:44.180
has family issues arise.

00:10:44.180 --> 00:10:48.480
Realizing that staying with his C-137 family
on Earth means he can't be a threat to national

00:10:48.480 --> 00:10:52.060
security, Rick tricks the president into thinking
things are good between them.

00:10:52.060 --> 00:10:53.060
Rick surrenders his place

00:10:53.060 --> 00:10:56.770
In light of Beth's personal struggles, Rick
offers her the chance to travel the galaxy

00:10:56.770 --> 00:11:00.900
on her own terms, while a clone version of
herself stays behind to take care of the family.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:04.710
"You could be gone a day, a week or the rest
of your life, with zero consequences.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.270
The moment you decide to come back, I flip
a switch, and the clone's job is done."

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:12.870
Unfortunately, this doesn't help with her
identity crisis, as now she has no clue if

00:11:12.870 --> 00:11:15.649
she's physically herself or a clone.

00:11:15.649 --> 00:11:19.240
Without meaning to, Rick pushes Beth right
back to Jerry, because he's the only one that

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:22.080
can help her understand if she's really herself.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:26.550
Jerry uses the opportunity to talk about the
first time that he told her he loved her.

00:11:26.550 --> 00:11:30.550
Realizing that his unconditional love is part
of who she is, she takes him back and endeavors

00:11:30.550 --> 00:11:34.410
to rebuild her family, without the manipulative
influence of Rick.

00:11:34.410 --> 00:11:37.270
The only way to do that, however, is to go
into hiding.

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:40.800
Unfortunately, none of the Smiths are smart
enough to hide from Rick, who arrives at their

00:11:40.800 --> 00:11:43.370
hideout ready to outright kill Jerry.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:46.460
But Beth puts her foot down with her father
for the first time.

00:11:46.460 --> 00:11:50.250
Rick tries to explain that Beth's feelings
are meaningless in a limitless multiverse,

00:11:50.250 --> 00:11:54.300
but he relents and yields his position as
the patriarch to stay with his family.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:56.490
"We're a real family now.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:12:00.589
In many ways, things will be like season one,
but more streamlined."

00:12:00.589 --> 00:12:02.839
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:12:02.839 --> 00:12:06.339
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
shows are coming soon.

00:12:06.339 --> 00:12:09.550
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

